solid lancet_tube_cap_PLACEHOLDER
# SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-W-2.0
# Copyright (c) 2026 Lambert iGEM 2025 Team and contributors
#
# THIS FILE IS A PLACEHOLDER. It does not contain printable mesh data.
# The real STL will be exported from the Fusion 360 parametric source
# and committed in the v0.1.0 release tagged for Zenodo archiving.
#
# Description of the intended part:
#
#   Part:     press-fit cartridge cap with reagent-loading port
#   Material: clear polycarbonate filament
#   Outer diameter:  ~12 mm (matches tube body)
#   Height:          ~6 mm
#   Loading port:    1.5 mm diameter through-hole, centered, to be
#                    sealed with a removable adhesive sticker after
#                    the patient sample is loaded
#   Friction-fit collar: 0.1 mm undersized to mate with the top
#                    compartment of `tube_body.stl`
#   Optical access:  the cap is printed in clear polycarbonate so the
#                    fluorescence reader can excite/emit through the
#                    cap face (485 nm excitation, 535 nm emission)
#
# Slicing parameters: same as `tube_body.stl` (0.1 mm layer height,
# 100 % infill, 260 C nozzle, 105 C bed). Anneal at 80 C for 30 min.
#
# To regenerate this file from the parametric source:
#   1. Open `tube_assembly.f3d` (forthcoming) in Autodesk Fusion 360.
#   2. Suppress the body component.
#   3. Right-click the cap component and choose Save As Mesh -> STL.
endsolid lancet_tube_cap_PLACEHOLDER
